              "type": "keyword",
              "ignore_above": 1024
            }
          }
        }
      }
    }
  },
  "_meta": {
    "managed_by": "redelk",
    "description": "The C2 field family, shared by rtops-*, implantsdb and credentials-* so that the file based C2s (through logstash) and the API based Mythic and Outflank C2 connectors cannot drift apart. c2.command.arguments and c2.implant are flattened: Sliver renames whole gRPC request and session objects into them, and without a bound the field count of rtops-* grows with every new Sliver command. c2.timestamp and implant.checkin are keywords rather than dates because the file based C2s write mutually incompatible free text there - Cobalt Strike's c2.timestamp has no year at all ('05/14 12:33:44') and its implant.checkin is a sentence ('host called home, sent: 16 bytes'); the parsed event time lives in @timestamp.",
    "authors": [
      "Outflank B.V. / Marc Smeets",
      "Lorenzo Bernardi (@fastlorenzo)"
    ]
  }
}
